  "id": "osf-review-failure-classification",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-10T10:01:03.558Z",
  "title": "Reviewer failure classification and honest verdicts",
  "summary": "This change makes a failed reviewer legible without ever echoing its text. A new `failure` module reads a reviewer's stdout/stderr and returns only a fixed category (credential, quota, model unavailable, schema rejected, unreachable, command line, permission, unknown), which is folded into the exit reason alongside the exit code and elapsed seconds. Timeouts become structured data (`Outcome::TimedOut` / `reviewers::Timeout`) carrying the binding limit, kill result, category and whether the run ever started, so reasons name the right limit and never claim a process was stopped when the kill failed. A run that made attempts and none answered now exits 2 after writing its `--out` file, and the posted review event follows the run's overall verdict: could-not-run posts COMMENT, never APPROVE. The reviewer home is always removed on drop, so CI no longer keeps or uploads it, and the answer schema sent to a harness drops `$schema`/`$id` while validation errors mask reviewer-chosen field names.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
